-- URBAN ECHO — Migration Notes & Frontend Compatibility Patch
-- File: supabase/safe_migration_notes.sql
--
-- This file documents every breaking change introduced in safe_setup.sql
-- and provides the corresponding frontend patch where needed.
-- DO NOT run this file blindly. Read each section first.
-- =============================================================================


-- =============================================================================
-- NOTE 1 — REF ID IS NOW GENERATED BY THE DATABASE TRIGGER
--
-- CHANGE: safe_setup.sql adds a BEFORE INSERT trigger (trg_complaint_ref_id)
--         that overwrites any ref_id sent by the frontend with a
--         sequence-generated value: UE-YYYY-XXXX.
--
-- FRONTEND IMPACT: SubmitComplaint.jsx (lines 87–93) currently:
--   1. Counts all complaints to derive a sequence number (race-prone).
--   2. Constructs ref_id = `UE-${year}-${String(seq).padStart(4,'0')}`.
--   3. Sends ref_id in the INSERT payload.
--   4. Reads it back from the INSERT response (data.ref_id).
--
-- AFTER THIS MIGRATION: The trigger generates ref_id. The frontend INSERT
--   can still send ref_id — the trigger will silently replace it.
--   The returned `data` from .select().single() will contain the REAL ref_id.
--   Step 4 (reading data.ref_id) already works correctly with no code change.
--
-- OPTIONAL CLEANUP (recommended, not required):
--   Remove lines 87–93 of SubmitComplaint.jsx (the COUNT query and manual
--   ref_id construction). The insert payload can omit ref_id entirely.
--   The success screen already reads success.refId from `data.ref_id`.
--   No other frontend change is required.
-- =============================================================================


-- =============================================================================
-- NOTE 2 — ANONYMOUS COMPLAINT PRIVACY FIX
--
-- CHANGE: The original complaint SELECT policy allowed any citizen to read
--         complaints where anonymous = TRUE. This exposed the content of
--         other citizens' anonymous complaints.
--
-- NEW POLICY: Citizens can only SELECT complaints where reporter_id = auth.uid().
--             Anonymous complaints (reporter_id IS NULL) are invisible to all
--             citizens. They are only visible to municipal_staff, admin, and
--             higher_official.
--
-- FRONTEND IMPACT:
--   - citizen/Dashboard.jsx and citizen/TrackComplaints.jsx query:
--       .eq('reporter_id', user.id)
--     When anonymous = TRUE, reporter_id is stored as NULL in the DB.
--     So anonymous complaints submitted by the citizen will NOT appear in
--     their own tracking dashboard after this fix.
--
--   If you want citizens to track their own anonymous complaints, two options:
--
--   OPTION A (recommended): Store the reporter_id even for anonymous complaints.
--     Change the frontend INSERT so reporter_id = user.id always.
--     Use a separate is_anonymous flag to hide the name from municipal staff UI.
--     Update ComplaintDetail.jsx to hide profile info when anonymous = TRUE
--     (it already does: "This complaint was submitted anonymously.").
--
--   OPTION B: Add a separate anon_token column (UUID) generated client-side,
--     stored locally, and used to claim the complaint later.
--
--   For the prototype, OPTION A is recommended. No RLS change needed for OPTION A.
--   The citizen_select policy (reporter_id = auth.uid()) works for both options.
-- =============================================================================


-- =============================================================================
