-- =============================================================================
-- NOTE 4 — STATUS HISTORY: DUAL-WRITE BEHAVIOUR
--
-- The safe_setup.sql trigger (trg_complaint_status_history) auto-records
-- status changes. ComplaintDetail.jsx also manually inserts a history row.
--
-- RESULT: Each status change will produce TWO history entries:
--   1. System entry (changed_by = NULL, remark = '[Auto] Status changed...')
--   2. Staff entry  (changed_by = user.id, remark = resolution notes or action)
--
-- This is NOT a bug — it provides a complete audit trail.
-- The citizen's TrackComplaints.jsx displays history rows with a null
-- changed_by gracefully (shows "Staff" when name is absent).
--
-- If you prefer a single entry per change:
--   Remove the manual insert from ComplaintDetail.jsx (lines 92–100).
--   Update the trigger to capture user context via app.settings.user_id
--   (requires SET LOCAL app.settings.user_id = auth.uid() before each update).
--   This is complex and not needed for the prototype.
-- =============================================================================


-- =============================================================================
-- NOTE 5 — PROFILE RLS: UPSERT FROM AUTHCONTEXT
--
-- AuthContext.jsx signUp() calls:
--   supabase.from('profiles').upsert({ id, full_name, email, phone, area, role: 'citizen' })
--
-- The new "profiles_insert_own" policy (WITH CHECK auth.uid() = id) allows this.
-- The upsert sends role: 'citizen' which is the only value the policy permits
-- (profiles_update_own WITH CHECK enforces role = get_my_role() on UPDATE).
--
-- IMPORTANT: Supabase upsert() uses INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE.
--   The UPDATE branch is governed by profiles_update_own which enforces
--   role = get_my_role(). Since 'citizen' === their current role, this passes.
--   A citizen cannot upsert role: 'admin' — the WITH CHECK will reject it.
-- =============================================================================


-- =============================================================================
-- NOTE 6 — EXECUTION CHECKLIST
--
-- Run in this order (all in one paste in the SQL Editor):
--
--   [1] Paste and run supabase/safe_setup.sql in Supabase SQL Editor.
--       Verify: No errors. "Success. No rows returned." is normal for DDL.
--
--   [2] Verify tables exist:
--       SELECT table_name FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema = 'public';
--       Expected: profiles, complaints, complaint_status_history, official_remarks
--
--   [3] Verify sequence exists:
--       SELECT * FROM information_schema.sequences WHERE sequence_name = 'complaint_ref_seq';
--
--   [4] Verify triggers:
--       SELECT tgname, tgrelid::regclass FROM pg_trigger WHERE tgname LIKE 'trg_%';
--       Expected: trg_complaint_ref_id, trg_profiles_updated_at,
--                 trg_complaints_updated_at, trg_complaint_status_history
--
--   [5] Verify RLS enabled:
--       SELECT tablename, rowsecurity FROM pg_tables WHERE schemaname = 'public';
--       All four tables should show rowsecurity = true.
--
--   [6] Verify helper functions:
--       SELECT public.get_my_role();   -- Returns NULL if not logged in (expected)
--
--   [7] Create storage bucket manually if the INSERT fails:
--       Dashboard → Storage → New Bucket → complaint-photos → Private → 5MB
--
--   [8] Set environment variables in .env:
--       VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
--       VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
--
--   [9] Promote staff/officials via SQL (Section 16 of safe_setup.sql).
--
--  [10] Test the full workflow:
--       Citizen registers → submits complaint → staff assigns + sets deadline
--       → deadline passes → official sees overdue complaint → adds remark.
-- =============================================================================
